All five items are done — the site is production-ready, the database is verified working, and everything is committed.

**Why signup/login "wasn't working":** it actually was. I probed the live endpoint and signup returns HTTP 200 with a confirmation email queued — but your project has **email confirmation enabled**, so a fresh account can't log in until the inbox link is clicked. Signed-up-but-unconfirmed accounts sit at "Invalid login credentials," which reads like a broken site. To prove the whole loop I confirmed a probe account directly in the database, then logged in through the real UI: sign-in worked, redirected to the dashboard, "Connected · RLS Active," stats rendering from real data. If you want one-click signup during testing, turn off "Confirm email" in Supabase → Authentication → Providers; for production, keep it on.

**One real database bug found and fixed:** the security section of [schema.sql](supabase/schema.sql) revoked all grants on `user_progress` but never restored the owner's, so even the rightful user got `403 permission denied` — the RLS policies existed but could never fire. Also, `service_role` had no table privileges whatsoever, meaning both Edge Functions would have failed on their first query. Applied the fix live and re-verified: owner reads own row (200), anonymous blocked (401), hidden tests blocked even when signed in (403).

**Dummy data removed:** the fabricated "Naman Rathi" profile in `data.js` (84-line demo layer, loaded on four pages) is gone, along with the renderers that consumed it. The landing page's score section now states the actual formula — 5 points per accepted problem, capped at 100, hash-chained evidence — instead of an example person's score. The database itself holds zero test rows: I deleted my probe account and its seed data, leaving only the 20-problem catalog and hidden test cases.

**Production blocker fixed:** every page was loading Tailwind from `cdn.tailwindcss.com`, which is a dev-only runtime and itself warns against production use. The per-page configs are ported into `@theme` tokens in [style.css](css/style.css), which now imports Tailwind for the Vite compiler, and the CDN `<script>` tags are removed from all 11 pages. Verified visually on landing, dashboard, and the problem arena — everything renders identically to before.

**Checks that all passed:** signup probe (200 + confirmation queued), browser login → dashboard flow, RLS isolation matrix, `Run` in the arena (starter code correctly fails, LOCAL/not-evidence label intact), `vite build` clean with no hidden-test needles or CDN references in `dist/`, console clean. Committed as two commits on `main`: `a6bae3d` (hidden-test extraction from the earlier turn) and `582c932` (this cleanup, 15 files, −748 lines). **Not pushed** — the remote is one commit behind, and pushing is your call.

Still outstanding: the two Edge Functions (`run-submission`, `verify-record`) remain undeployed, so submissions stay local-only until they're live with a Judge0 key.
