## The helper

[utils.js](js/utils.js) exports `escapeHtml(value)` that escapes `& < > " '` (quotes included, so it's safe inside attributes too), and also registers `window.escapeHtml` for the *classic* inline scripts that can't use ES imports.

## Changed — every user/localStorage/Supabase-sourced interpolation

**[js/auth.js](js/auth.js)** (imports the helper) — navbar auth slots, 4 interpolations: `initials`, and `user.name || user.username` in the desktop badge, the desktop dropdown ("Signed in as"), and the mobile menu. These come from Supabase Auth `user_metadata`, set from the signup form — anything a user typed at signup flows here.

**[js/main.js](js/main.js)** (imports the helper):
- Recent Activity feed: `a.text` (embeds the submission's `problemTitle`/`problemId` + language from Supabase), `a.badge` (language/difficulty from Supabase), and `a.time` defensively.
- Dashboard "Recently Solved": `item.title`, `item.difficulty`, `item.runtime`, and `item.id` — persisted in localStorage by ProgressTracker, so tamperable; the id also goes through `encodeURIComponent` in the href.

**[evidence.html](evidence.html)** (head loads utils.js; both sites are in its classic script and call `window.escapeHtml`):
- Accepted-problem records: `s.problemTitle || s.problemId`, `s.language`, `s.difficulty`, `s.runtime` — Supabase submission rows — plus `s.recordId` which is interpolated into the `data-record-id` **attribute** (quote-escaping matters there).
- Add-Evidence preview card: `name`, `detail`, `skill` — typed straight into the form fields; the highest-risk XSS in the app since submission is instant definition.

**[profile.html](profile.html)** (imports the helper in its module script) — Projects & assessments grid: `e.name`, `e.skill`, `e.detail`, `e.timestamp` — user evidence assembled from localStorage records + Supabase rows (see `getUserEvidence` in user-stats.js).

**[skill.html](skill.html)** (imports the helper) — Timeline of accepted submissions: `title` (`problemTitle`/`problemId`) and the difficulty inside `cat` — Supabase rows.

**[problem.html](problem.html)**:
- Submissions list: `s.status` and `s.runtime` — written into localStorage rows on submit, sourced from server responses.
- Run-results drawer: `currCase.error` in both the hidden-case and visible-case branches, plus `currCase.status` in the hidden branch and `currCase.userOutputDisplay` in the visible one — these echo output/runtime errors produced by executing *the user's own code*, in both the local and server-graded paths.
- Also cleaned up: the page had **two** local `escapeHtml` definitions (the second silently shadowing the first) and both only escaped `& < >` — no quotes, which mattered since `recordId` goes into an attribute. They're now one thin wrapper that delegates to the shared implementation in utils.js; all call paths verified to run after the deferred head modules execute (DOMContentLoaded async init and click handlers only), so `window.escapeHtml` is always present.

## Deliberately left alone — with reasons

- **problem.html catalog renders** (`prob.description`, examples `input/output/explanation`, constraints, hints, `prob.editorial`, sample test-case `inputDisplay`/`expectedDisplay`, `prob.number`): written by the author in problems-data.js, never user-touched. `description`/`editorial` are *intentionally* HTML (rich formatting), which is only safe because the catalog is trusted content.
- **problem-list.html table rows**: every cell (`p.number`, `p.title`, `p.category`, `p.acceptance`, `p.difficulty`) is static catalog data.
- **main.js skill rings/cards + weak area** (`s.name`, `s.id`): derived from the skills config in js/skills.js.
- **evidence.html skill options `<select>`** (`window.KredoraSkills.skillOptions`): config-driven.
- **main.js achievements feed** (`ach.label`/`ach.date`): fixed milestone strings plus numeric counters.
- **problem.html line-number gutter** (numeric), run/submit button spinners (static markup), `logs` box (rendered via `textContent`, safe by construction).
- **Fixed-enum labels** (`stateLabel`, `typeLabel`, `icon`, difficulty-color classes, `badgeClass`): constants, no data flows into them.
- **[dashboard.html](dashboard.html)**: has zero `innerHTML` assignments — all its dynamic content is rendered by main.js, which is now covered.

## Verification

- `vite build` passes (all bundles and inline module scripts parsed).
- The two edited classic inline scripts (problem.html, evidence.html) were extracted and syntax-checked with `node --check` — both OK.

